# Headers for every static asset response (the pages, /admin/*, /resultados,
# fonts, the favicon). wrangler's assets binding serves these *before* the
# Worker script runs (DEC-020), so Hono middleware never sees these requests —
# see backend/src/http/middleware/security-headers.ts for the Worker-side twin
# of this file, which covers /records, /api/public/*, /health and the 404
# passthrough instead.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy here carries ONLY frame-ancestors. Every other
# CSP directive (script-src, style-src, object-src, etc.) is set per-page by
# Astro's own `security.csp` (astro.config.mjs) as a <meta> tag, hashed
# against that page's actual inline scripts/styles on every build. A browser
# enforces two CSPs as their INTERSECTION, not a merge — keeping the resource
# directives in exactly one place is what keeps this policy readable instead
# of two overlapping, driftable lists. frame-ancestors is here specifically
# because a <meta> CSP cannot carry it at all (the directive is ignored
# outside a real header) — this file exists for that one directive, not out
# of a general preference for headers over meta tags. See DEC-030.
#
# No `preload` on HSTS: preload is a submission to browser vendors that is
# effectively irreversible, and is the developer's call to make, not
# something this file ships silently.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
